H is different in kind. It requires a chain of anachronistic syncretism with no documentary footprint:
* Kuji-in/kujiho are nine Buddhist/Shingon hand seals, not thirteen black/white glyphs and not linked to Hindu chakras;
* Chakras, Taoist erotic energy rituals for perception/mind influence, and a “nine holes of the female body” anatomical numerology are not attested in Edo ninjutsu or Bansenshukai scholarship;
* The explanation re-labels the circles as the intended content rather than explaining why kanji are absent from every transcription, and it cannot account for the 15-symbol pattern vs. nine seals.

The erotic-anatomical, chakra-Taoist reading of Kuji-in is modern pop-esotericism projected back onto a practical military manual. It has no contemporary source, no scribal error type, and no explanatory power for a uniform lacuna. That makes it the least historically and logically coherent explanation.

